  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader reaching the end of a page, I want the page bubble (« 208 / 227 ») in its **own pill, centred** in the bottom bar, so that the page position stands apart from the actions instead of being grouped with « Actualiser » and « Répondre ».\n\n### Observed (operator, iPhone, 2026-11-16, build cd049542)\n\n- At the end of a page, the bottom bar shows ‹ and › on the left, then **one** grouped pill on the right holding « 208 / 227 », the refresh button and the compose button.\n- Wanted: « N / M » in a separate pill, centred horizontally. ‹ › stay on the left; refresh and compose stay on the right in their own pill.\n- Screenshot kept locally by the operator (it shows member pseudos, so it is not attached).\n\n### Scope\n\n- `ReaderBottomBar` / `ReaderPageControls` (#932, #820): the layout of the end-of-page state. VoiceOver (where the bubble is always shown) follows the same layout.\n- The hint « Tirer vers le haut pour actualiser » is unchanged.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] At the end of a page, « N / M » is a separate, centred pill. It still opens the page menu (#924).\n- [ ] A test on the bar's layout state fails without the change.\n- [ ] Device check in the operator's general review: iPhone portrait and landscape, iPad.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
